# Dependency Alignment + Run-All-Setup Flow

## Rule

When changing dependencies across the workspace:

1. **Run version alignment first** — `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/repo-management/run-version-alignment.sh`
2. **If misaligned** — `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/repo-management/run-version-alignment.sh --fix`
3. **Then run setup** — `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/repo-management/run-all-setup.sh`
4. **Commit uv.lock** — run-all-setup updates uv.lock via setup.sh; commit and push so agents/CI get identical deps

## uv.lock

- **setup.sh** runs `uv lock` when pyproject.toml is newer than uv.lock
- **run-all-setup** runs setup.sh per repo → updates uv.lock everywhere deps changed
- **uv.lock is committed** (never in .gitignore) — agents pull it via git
- After run-all-setup, commit any changed uv.lock files

